{"question": "Does Fidelity charge fees on a Trump Account?", "answer": "Fidelity has not published any fees for Trump Accounts, because as of October 2026 only Robinhood Securities, LLC, the trustee chosen by the [U.S. Treasury](https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0642), can hold one. Fidelity plans to accept Trump Account rollovers once Treasury publishes formal operating guidance, and that guidance was still unpublished on October 8, 2026. For now, Robinhood's [Trump Account customer agreement](https://cdn.robinhood.com/assets/robinhood/legal/trump_account_customer_agreement.pdf) dated September 30, 2026 says Robinhood charges no other account fees to maintain the balance and no fee to transfer out."}